Z||000000||mshill||09-30-1999||12:44 AM||||Were talking 86 V6 SE here...<P>I now have two dogbones...<P>The stock one, from which I removed the bushings to find that the Poly bushings I purchased won't fit in it is about 7 inches long (4 3/4 inches center to center of bushings).<P>The one Tom sent me (thanks, it got here) which the new poly bushings fit but is 6 inches long (3 3/4 inches center to center of bushings).<P>So, can I use the short one?  Will the 1 inch difference put stress on the engine mounts or cradle mounts?||||reg||9
Z||000001||batboy||09-30-1999||01:01 AM||||I didn't know there were two different size V6 dogbones. I know the 2.5 dogbones are much longer than the V6 ones. Maybe a previous owner put the wrong one on off another type of car. I just installed a new ultimate dogbone onto my 85 GT with the 2.8 engine, tonight. The old one and new one are both 6 inches long. Maybe that's why the new poly bushings won't fit your old one, it's the wrong doggyboner.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||09-30-1999||01:53 AM||||It's possible that a previous owner (I am the third) could have switched dogbones. I cannot imagine why.  Especially since they didn't do any of their own work on the car.  Who knows?<P>I am going to try and put it in when I get the front end back together and off the jackstands.<P>||||reg||10
Z||000003||TOM||09-30-1999||11:15 AM||||Yes all V6 dog bones are the same. The shorter one. The one I sent you is the same as the one on my 86 V6 SE. When you put it in it will seem a little short. You will have to pull the engine back a bit to get the bolt in but it is the right one.||||reg||1
